# Cell from playpick: mode=walk, boss=gift (coverage label only -- evening
# steers at no boss, the walk starts at the door same as any other), spec
# druid:restoration, style=flee, size=10, difficulty=normal, view=844x390,
# touch, save=carried (behaves as fresh per #273 -- the dev-server port is
# pid-derived so localStorage never actually carries across separate
# playbot invocations).
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl and direction.md's hypothesis #6/#281 first.
# druid:restoration has been played five times before (grep: mash x3,
# auto x2) and never once inside mode=walk or mode=clear -- this is its
# first evening, full stop. It also lands on a hypothesis with eleven
# prior confirmations: every fresh 10-normal evening that has gone through
# cross()'s own THE VIGIL crossing has either stalled in place or been
# caught by the corridor's watchmen and wiped, regardless of style, and a
# wipe there leaves PULL AGAIN unable to restart the fight (#271). flee has
# already wiped this exact size/difficulty twice before (hunter:
# marksmanship, paladin:holy) -- druid's own moveSpeed (167) sits between
# those two classes' speeds (173, 158), so this is the first data point
# that can tell whether the one style/class pairing that crossed clean
# (melee on the fastest class, rogue at 178) was really about raw speed or
# something else: if 167 also gets caught, speed alone does not explain
# the one clean pass.
open
tap raid
tap next
tap class:druid:restoration
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

evening flee 240 8
state
shot after-evening
says
bill
